      },
      {
        "does": "The black gear low on the side of the trailer's front winds the landing gear's two legs, with their little wheels, down to the ground and back up.",
        "source": "book: step 68 on page 296 (the arrows on the gear and the legs), page 421 (the gear marked at the trailer's front)",
        "control": "p1706 18575",
        "moves": [
          "p1723 42610",
          "p1724 42610"
        ]
      },
      {
        "does": "One of the two black gears at the trailer's rear works both cranes' large linear actuators together, swinging each crane's long leg out until it stands on the ground beside the trailer and back in: a shaft runs forward under the deck through constant velocity joints from the rear crane to the front one.",
        "source": "book: bag 6 crane steps (the large actuators and the long shafts, page 342 shows the shafts plugging in); page 421 (middle photo, the arrow along the leg; the rear gear marked)",
        "control": "p2080 18575",
        "moves": [
          "p1958 61927-f1",
