        ],
        "note": "which of the two rear gears works which crane function is inferred from the model's shafts"
      },
      {
        "does": "The other black gear at the trailer's rear works both cranes' small linear actuators together, swinging each crane's green arm up and over to lift the container on its four chains, and back: a row of five 16 tooth gears under the deck passes the turn across to a second shaft that runs to both cranes, where bevel gears and universal joints take it up to each actuator.",
        "source": "book: bag 5 steps 15-24 (the row of gears, pages 268-271), bag 6 crane steps; page 421 (right photo, the arrows on the arm and the leg)",
        "control": "p2079 18575",
        "moves": [
